<p><span style="text-decoration: line-through;">Was asked to take another look, will crit soon.</span></p>
<p>Yeah you're going in the right direction, definitely. I'm not sure the reveal is coherent/clever enough to carry the article, though, and I'd suggest taking something more in the vein of what Voct suggested below. You know, like, you're reading this weird little article and you realize it's the Earth's digestive tract (?) and&#8230; what's that really mean? Why's that cool?</p>
<p>Also minor note: Might still want to tone down the &quot;addiction&quot; component to be a sort of side-effect instead of something major. Flushing wedding rings and describing it as an addiction isn't particularly charming or interesting, but the idea of employees &quot;running the water&quot; as Riemann described is.</p>
<p>Regardless, you seem to know how this goes. I'll <strong><span style="color: green">greenlight</span></strong> this idea, best of luck.</p>

